# Extension MCP contribution

## Manifest files

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `sedea.mcp-contribution.schema.json` | JSON Schema (v0.1) for contribution shape |
| `sedea.mcp-contribution.example.json` | Starter example — copy to `sedea.mcp-contribution.json` when ready |
| `sedea.mcp-contribution.json` | Authoritative manifest for this extension (create when servers are defined) |

## Required shape (floor)

Top-level **required** keys: `extensionId`, `version`, `servers`.

Each server entry must declare **`transport`**: `stdio` or `sse` per the schema enum.

## Runtime registration boundary

| Phase | MCP registration |
|-------|------------------|
| **Develop / scaffold** | Manifest authoring only — no Mission Control aggregator write |
| **Install on packaged Sedea** | **Install Sedea Extension** mission writes `extensionContributions` |

**Forbidden:** using **sedea-mcp-hub** as the extension-native MCP registry. Hub is for external REST/API bridges only.

## Sedea MCP Hub appendix

External API bridges belong in **sedea-mcp-hub** — not in this extension's stdio/SSE contribution manifest. See `AGENTS.md` in this repo for the platform split.
